# {{name}}: the shape of a client's .env. The real file lives in
# ${{env_prefix}}_DATA_DIR/.env (chmod 600), never in this checkout.
# Placeholders only: the CI secret scan skips this file, so never paste a
# real value here. `{{cli}} doctor` shows where each value came from.

# Never here: {{env_prefix}}_CONFIRM_CODE_SECRET (the relayed-code secret),
# CONSOLE_SECRET, KIT_TTY, KIT_SKILL_PACK_ROOT, PYTHON*, LD_*, DYLD_*. The skill pack
# never loads them from a file (kit/env.py) and doctor names such a line. Set
# the confirm-code secret in the process env of what runs the gate (the
# console, or the agent relaying codes through chat); unset, confirming
# needs a terminal.

# Writes stay off until the owner agrees in writing, with a cap:
# {{env_prefix}}_ALLOW_WRITES=1
